# Grandfathered childop files that issue raw syscalls without a complete
# childop_direct_syscalls_add() accounting chain.
#
# Two namespaced categories:
#
# UNCOUNTED:<file> — file-level: the translation unit calls raw-syscall
# functions (trinity_raw_syscall(), socket(), sendmsg(), sendto(),
# setsockopt(), mmap(), syscall()) but does not call
# childop_direct_syscalls_add().  Many of these route netlink-path
# syscalls through the nl_* transport which calls
# childop_direct_syscalls_add() internally at nl_close(); own-body calls
# outside that transport remain uncounted.
#
# THREAD_UNCOUNTED:<file>#<fn> — worker-thread level: the file IS wired at
# the op-body level (calls childop_direct_syscalls_add()) but contains a
# static void * pthread worker function <fn> that issues raw syscalls
# without accumulating them back into the parent's direct_calls tally.
# Each worker gets its own baseline slot so that new workers added to an
# already-baselined file are caught immediately.
#
# FORK_UNCOUNTED:<file>#<fn> — fork-worker level: the file IS wired but
# contains a static void fork-child body <fn> (detected by presence of
# _exit() without an internal fork() call) that issues raw syscalls
# without a ->syscall/tally/count accumulation visible to the scanner.
# Like THREAD_UNCOUNTED, each worker gets its own slot.  Fix by adding
# a shared-memory tally (shm is MAP_SHARED) or by wiring the worker
# to call childop_direct_syscalls_add() before _exit().
#
# The UNCOUNTED list should shrink over time as each file is wired.
# THREAD_UNCOUNTED and FORK_UNCOUNTED entries should be fixed by proper
# per-worker tally wiring.  Never grow any of these lists.
UNCOUNTED:childops/fs/hfs-mount-fuzz.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/bareudp-rx.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/bridge-fdb-stp-traffic.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/bridge-fdb-stp-vlan-mass.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/crafted-icmp-rx.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/esp-crafted-rx-frag.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/esp-crafted-rx-stacked.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/geneve-rx.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/ip_gre-churn.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/netfilter/nfnl-util.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/netfilter/nftables/fwd.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/netfilter/nftables/l4frag.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/netlink/genl-util.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/netlink/nl80211-churn-discovery.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/psp-key-rotate-devlink-port.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/psp-key-rotate-lifecycle.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/sctp-chunk-rx.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/veth-asymmetric-xdp.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/xfrm/xfrm-churn-compat-sweep.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/xfrm/xfrm-churn-pfkey.c
UNCOUNTED:childops/net/xfrm/xfrm-churn-traffic.c
# Newly surfaced by extended fork-worker detection (t439): these workers use
# __attribute__((noreturn)) on the same line as the static void signature, or
# terminate via syscall(__NR_exit) rather than bare _exit(), making them
# invisible to the previous _exit()-only predicate. All files are wired at
# the op-body level; the fork-child raw-syscall budget is not yet propagated
# back into the parent's direct_calls tally. Wiring is a separate concern.

# Newly surfaced by quantitative tally predicate (fn_tally_count < fn_raw_sites)
# and widened raw-syscall regex (raw_[a-z_]+ file-local wrappers).  Workers
# previously passing with a single tally reference despite multiple raw-syscall
# sites are now correctly flagged.  All files are wired at the op-body level;
# per-worker tally coverage is the outstanding gap.
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/net/sockmap-cork-race.c#sender_thread
# Newly surfaced by widened function-entry detection (bool NAME(struct childdata *child)
# and static int NAME(void *arg) shapes): 28 entries previously invisible to the scanner.
# These are the primary childop entry functions and _in_ns clone bodies; all files are
# wired at op-body level or unwired. Per-function tally coverage is the outstanding gap.
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/fs/hfs-mount-fuzz.c#hfs_mount_in_ns
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/fs/hfs-mount-fuzz.c#hfs_mount_fuzz
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/fs/statmount-idmap-overflow.c#statmount_idmap_loop_in_ns
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/io_uring/flood.c#iouring_flood
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/io_uring/net-multishot.c#iouring_net_multishot
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/mm/mremap-merge-matrix.c#mremap_merge_matrix
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/mm/uffd-churn.c#uffd_churn
THREAD_UNCOUNTED:childops/net/af-alg-template-probe.c#af_alg_template_probe
